<title>INDIA: India 96/97 copper cathodes output 38,389 tonnes.</title>
<headline>India 96/97 copper cathodes output 38,389 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's state-run Hindustan Copper Ltd (HCL) produced 38,389 tonnes of copper cathodes in 1996/97 (April-March), down from 41,153 tonnes in the previous fiscal year, the Mines Ministry said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The ministry said in a statement that HCL produced 4,150 tonnes of copper cathodes in March 1997 against a target of 4,500 tonnes.</p>
<p>HCL also produced 3,050 tonnes of continous cast copper rods in March against a target of 3,000 tonnes, the statement said.</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>	    Installed  March, 1997   Cumulative output</p>
<p>	    capacity   -----------   -----------------</p>
<p>	    (annual)     Actual	Apr-Mar 96/97  Apr-Mar 95/96</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------- Copper</p>
<p> cathodes   47,500	 4,150	 38,389	 41,153</p>
<p>Copper</p>
<p> rods	 60,000	 3,050	 41,390	 37,316</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures are in tonnes and provisional.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91 11 301 2024</p>
</text>
